{
  "_comment": [
    "Project-scoped MCP registration for the seedgraph server. Copy to `.mcp.json`",
    "at the root of the working directory you want the server available in, then",
    "edit `command` and the `--root` value for your machine.",
    "",
    "PREREQUISITE: `pip install -e \".[mcp]\"` in the SAME interpreter named by",
    "`command` below. Without the extra the command exits 1 with an install hint.",
    "",
    "`command` must be the interpreter that has the extra. Backslashes are doubled",
    "because this is JSON. A venv python is the usual answer on Windows.",
    "",
    "`--root` pins the seedgraph projects home. Prefer this flag over a SEEDGRAPH_HOME",
    "env var: MCP hosts pass a filtered environment to the child process, so an env",
    "var may not survive; the flag always does. Omit it to use the default home.",
    "",
    "Add \"--redact-private\" to `args` to blank full-text-derived fields (span and",
    "claim text, `ask` citation quotes) for non-shareable works. Best-effort valve,",
    "not the load-bearing access gate. See docs/USER_HANDBOOK.md section 10.",
    "",
    "Remove this _comment key before use if your host is strict about unknown fields."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "seedgraph": {
      "command": "D:\\documents\\research\\seedgraph_v2\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe",
      "args": [
        "-m",
        "seedgraph",
        "mcp",
        "serve",
        "--root",
        "C:\\Users\\<you>\\.seedgraph"
      ]
    }
  }
}
